        "original_id": "5cc0e856-b43c-545e-a595-b9621bee980c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: La jolie fille de Perth, Mitridate, re di Ponto, La dame blanche, Lucia di Lammermoor, I puritani\n- People: Georges Bizet, Jules-Henri Vernoy de Saint-Georges, Jules Adenis, Sir Walter Scott, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Concepts: opera, opera seria, musical influence, libretto, novel adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Mitridate, re di Ponto, K. 87 (74a), is an early opera seria in three acts by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.\n- La jolie fille de Perth (The Fair Maid of Perth) is an opera in four acts by Georges Bizet.\n- La jolie fille de Perth has a libretto by Jules-Henri Vernoy de Saint-Georges and Jules Adenis.\n- La jolie fille de Perth is based on a novel by Sir Walter Scott.\n- The musical style of La dame blanche heavily influenced the later operas Lucia di Lammermoor, I puritani, and La jolie fille de Perth.",
